Prerequisites
The notes assume basic quantum mechanics and the circuit model: Dirac notation, Pauli matrices, density matrices, expectation values and their statistical error.
The tutorials are Jupyter notebooks in Python, which run in Google Colab. They assume basic Python (variables, functions, loops, lists and dictionaries) and a little familiarity with Jupyter notebooks, NumPy arrays and Matplotlib plots. If any of these is new to you, these short introductions cover what we need:

Python: the official Python tutorial, sections 3 to 5;
Jupyter notebooks in Colab: Overview of Colab;
NumPy: NumPy: the absolute basics for beginners;
Matplotlib: Quick start guide.
